Hypothesis: When replacing an existing dataset entry that previously held the cached minimum or maximum range value, the method calls updateBounds(), but updateBounds() only resets cached min/max fields to NaN and does not recompute bounds from all existing items. The rest of add() then only incorporates the newly added item, causing the global minimum to be lost if it moved to another cell. In the failing test, replacing R1,C1 removes cached min 8.5 from that cell, but another item at R2,C1 still has min 8.5; the method incorrectly sets minimumRangeValue to the new item's 8.6.

